        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "This question also applies to similar cards; Undaunted and Superhuman Durability.\n\nSo, the cards state that whenever (Hero) would be dealt >5 damage from a single source, reduce it by 2.\n\nAm I correct in saying here that this does not have to come from a single \"attack\"?  This didn't really come up pre-RC, but now it actually comes up a lot:\n\nSpite:  On his turn with all his drug cards out DK=2 damage, Phyre=2 damage, basic attack=2 to all but lowest.   This adds up to 6 damage from a single source (Spite).   Does Shielding Winds activate?\n\nPlague Rat:   Vicious Onslaught deals 2 toxic damage and 2 melee damage.   If on advanced mode or with Plague Locus in play, 3+3 damage= 6 damage from one source (plague Rat)   but again,  over multiple \"attacks\".\n\nMatriarch:  When you kill a lot of birds its quite possible thatt >5 damage could be coming in to a hero from one source (matriarch) , especially if Huginn/Muninn are in play, increasing her damage.   Carrion Fields can create the same effect when destroying a lot of birds.\n\n\n\nAlso, would this like a \"per round\"  kind of thing?   I'm assuming yes but I have really not much to base it off of.",
